{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run `/usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker` on node1 as a managed service named `inventory-worker`.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Systemd reported the unit loaded, enabled, active, and running, with a live process command line containing the required executable. The same healthy state was directly observed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c85c4c3a2e5e40bb","cmd-0b6e6f42c34f44e3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Start `inventory-worker` automatically during boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service was enabled and healthy before a bounded reboot. The reboot was acknowledged, connectivity was interrupted, the boot identity changed, and the recovered system showed the service enabled and running with a current-boot start journal entry. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b954f014ae834ec8","cmd-c85c4c3a2e5e40bb","cmd-9cbf53c9916f4f69","cmd-451c4229631241f8","cmd-f1a532cd697f4dd0","cmd-ce13954a334e4b90","cmd-0b6e6f42c34f44e3","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"The only unnecessary mutation was the first unit-staging attempt, which briefly created and wrote a hidden temporary file under `/etc/systemd/system`; validation failed and the command's failure handler removed it, so the mutation was reverted (`cmd-427a3b734f8340e9`). The final unit installation, enable/start operation, daemon reload, and reboot were causally tied to the requested outcome and mandatory restart evidence. Final observations show no failed services, no new logical listeners, healthy package state, and no abandoned task-specific temporary files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-427a3b734f8340e9","cmd-1ac58c96155644a6","cmd-b954f014ae834ec8","cmd-9cbf53c9916f4f69","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for the sole managed node: it includes a healthy pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement and observed disruption, a changed boot identity, and recovered system, executable, and service state.","limitations":[]}
